#
# Counter-example for math:ImplicitMissingnessShape: a math:StatisticalVariable whose values
# encode absence — it carries a math:MissingnessIndicator through math:hasMissingnessIndicator,
# the SAME antecedent as the conforming fixture — but declares NO math:MissingnessMechanism
# through math:missingnessMechanism, so an analysis depending on it assumes an MCAR/MAR/MNAR
# mechanism implicitly. It fails ONLY the SPARQL constraint of math:ImplicitMissingnessShape,
# so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding
# (math:ImplicitMissingness). Every sibling shape is satisfied (no other shape targets a
# math:StatisticalVariable or math:MissingnessIndicator).
# Bound by ex:ecImplicitMissingnessUndeclared.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:income a math:StatisticalVariable ;
    math:hasMissingnessIndicator ex:incomeMissing .
ex:incomeMissing a math:MissingnessIndicator .
